<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hawaii</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hawaiian Islands</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hawaii is an archipelago in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a> and, since 1959, the 50th state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a>. Settled by Polynesian voyagers probably between about 1000 and 1200 CE, its islands were ruled by rival chiefdoms until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-i">Kamehameha I</a> united them as the Kingdom of Hawaii by 1810. The kingdom was overthrown in 1893, and the islands were annexed by the United States in 1898.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hawaii.jpg" alt="Hawaii" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dbenbenn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hawaii.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
